<section>
  <div class="card reveal">
    <p>Dana grew up in Syria, where the sound of gunfire and drones overhead were simply part of daily life, and where her father had to leave the country just to provide for the family. A decade later, she graduated from a Canadian university with honours.</p>
    <p class="quote">"The community and the professors were so supportive — I met my best friends here."</p>
    <p>Before law, Dana actually considered becoming an actor. She chose a different path for the stability it could offer her family: her father, once a doctor, and her mother, once a teacher, gave up their careers to bring the family to Canada.</p>
    <p class="quote">"It's our turn," she says of honoring that sacrifice.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="section-title reveal">Her passion: wrongful convictions</h2>
  <p class="section-sub reveal">Two classes at Carleton changed the direction of her career.</p>
  <div class="card reveal">
    <p>Dana discovered how frequent, devastating, and life-altering wrongful convictions can be — and it reshaped how she sees the criminal justice system. Her focus going forward: how wrongful convictions specifically affect women and their families.</p>
    <div class="chip">Wrongful Convictions</div>
    <div class="chip">Criminal Law</div>
    <div class="chip">Women & Justice</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="section-title reveal">What's next</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-2">
    <div class="card reveal">
      <h3>🎓 M.A. at Carleton</h3>
      <p style="margin-top:8px; color:var(--ink-soft);">Starting this September, with hopes of a PhD — and one day, teaching at Carleton herself.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card reveal">
      <h3>📣 Law Ambassador</h3>
      <p style="margin-top:8px; color:var(--ink-soft);">Created content for the department's social media and connected with prospective students and their families at events.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

